  "bio": "State Representative Steve Toth is a small business owner representing South Montgomery County in the Texas House of Representatives. Steve and his wife, Babette, have lived in The Woodlands area for 26 years. In the Texas House, Rep. Toth has successfully passed laws addressing county government ethics reform, parental visitation rights at schools, the elimination of Critical Race Theory in the classroom, and access to educational tools for students with dyslexia, to name a few. Having served on the powerful Appropriations Committee since 2019, Rep. Toth has helped craft three budgets for Texas – the state with the 9th largest economy in the world. In 2023, Rep. Toth earned one of only four Taxpayer Champion awards designated by Texans for Fiscal.",
